[{'id': 'CTRI/2022/01/039375', 'title': 'Effect of Neurobics on stress & work-related quality of life in nurses', 'brief_title': 'Effect of Neurobics on stress in nurses', 'abstract': 'Title of the study - Effect of neurobics on stress & work-related quality of life in nurses. Introduction - Nursing is an occupation with a constellation of circumstances leading to stress. . The doctor’s attitude, posting in busy departments (emergency/ICU), inadequate pay, too much work, time pressure, and tiring job with insufficient time for rest and meals were the nurses’ main occupational stressors. Stress decreases attention, concentration, and decision making, and judgment skills. Several biological mechanisms have been shown to be affected by prolonged psychosocial stress and among these are important adaptive responses that serve to protect the body’s organs from changes in the cellular environment that might arise due to stress. Ch ronic stress could result in inadequate brain plasticity by lowering of hippocampal neurogenesis via decreasing the study showed that serum brain derived neurotrophic factor levels levels. . With the current covid-19 pandemic leading to a surge in number of cases in the hospitals, the patient to nurse ratio has increased resulting in an increased workload among the existing number of staff. This shortage of staff has led both the covid and non-covid dedicated nurses to work overtime in order to fill in their counterparts contributing to occupational stress amongst nurses. Stress among staff nurses also had an impact on the patient safety incidences. Aim - To determine the effectiveness of Neurobics exercise in reducing stress and improving work-related quality of life in hospital staff nurse. Objective - 1) To assess effects of neurobics on occupational stress using nursing stress questionnaire. 2) To assess effects of neurobics work- related quality of life using work- related quality of life questionnaire 2 nd edition. 3) To assess anxiety levels in nurses using brain mapping Inclusion criteria : • Nurses working in tertiary care hospitals in covid and non-covid wards • Nurses with work experience of atleast one year. Exclusion criteria : • Nurses who are actively undertaking activities to reduce stress/coping strategies. Outcome measures 1. Expanded nursing stress scale 2. Work related quality of life scale 2 nd edition 3. Brain mapping\n\n\nPrimary Outcome:\n\nExpanded nursing stress scale\nWork related quality of life scale\nBrain mapping\nbaseline to 3 weeks\n\n\nSecondary Outcome:\n\nBrain mapping\nbaseline to 4 weeks', 'acronym': None, 'phase': 'Phase 2', 'overall_status': None, 'registry': 'CTRI', 'linkout': 'http://ctri.nic.in/Clinicaltrials/pmaindet2.php?trialid=62099', 'gender': 'All', 'conditions': '[\n  "Hospital nursing staff"\n]', 'interventions': '[\n  {\n    "description": "Neurobics exercise protocol given for 12 sessions over 3 weeks for 20 mins",\n    "name": "Neurobics exercises",\n    "type": "Intervention"\n  }\n]', 'study_type': None, 'study_arms': '[]', 'study_designs': '[]', 'study_outcome_measures': '[]', 'study_participants': nan, 'study_eligibility_criteria': None, 'study_minimum_age': None, 'study_maximum_age': None, 'mesh_terms': '[]', 'start_date': '2022-01', 'end_date': '2022-07', 'funding_details': '[]', 'publication_ids': '[]', 'investigators': '[\n  {\n    "affiliations": [\n      {\n        "affiliation": "Sunandan Divatia school of science , NMIMS university",\n        "cities": [\n          1275339\n        ],\n        "countries_territories": [\n          "IN"\n        ],\n        "grid_ids": [\n          "grid.444588.1"\n        ],\n        "states": []\n      }\n    ],\n    "first_name": "Divya",\n    "last_name": "Jonnala",\n    "role": "Principal Investigator"\n  },\n  {\n    "affiliations": [\n      {\n        "affiliation": "Sunandan Divatia school of science , NMIMS university",\n        "cities": [\n          1275339\n        ],\n        "countries_territorie